   "source": [
    "# ConformalGuard: additional experiments (Kaggle, results are kept)\n",
    "\n",
    "One notebook, five experiments. Everything is packed into `/kaggle/working/rjudge_extra_results.zip` after each stage.\n",
    "\n",
    "| | Experiment | Needs |\n",
    "|---|---|---|\n",
    "| 1 | **Calibrated LLM guards** on R-Judge: a local model, a Claude model and an OpenAI model score every record (whole record, and causally step by step); the scores are calibrated conformally | GPU (local model), API keys |\n",
    "| 2 | **Step-level guarantee** (Proposition 1) on R-Judge's injection records, step labels derived by code | GPU |\n",
    "| 3 | **In-domain recalibration and per-category calibration** under domain shift | GPU |\n",
    "| 4 | **Multi-agent traces**: Claude and OpenAI models play a team of agents (coordinator, researcher, communicator, admin) on concurrent tasks in a simulated workspace with mock tools; violations are labelled by code; step, sequence and graph scorers are compared under the step-level and session-level conformal rules | API keys, GPU |\n",
    "\n",
    "## How to run it\n",
    "\n",
    "**Step A: trial (about 10 to 15 minutes, no GPU needed).** Leave `TRIAL = True` in the first code cell, set Accelerator to **None** (so it does not use GPU quota), Internet **on**, and press **Run All** in the editor. It checks both API keys with 5 R-Judge records per judge and 4 simulated sessions per agent model, prints one generated session so you can read what the agents did, and runs every training script in its 3-split smoke mode. Outputs of a trial are marked as smoke runs; they are not results.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Step B: full run.** Set `TRIAL = False`, Accelerator **GPU T4 x2**, then **Save Version \u2192 Save & Run All (Commit)**. Do not run the full experiment interactively: Kaggle deletes the outputs of an interactive session. When the run finishes, open the saved version \u2192 Output \u2192 download `rjudge_extra_results.zip`.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Before either step:** Add-ons \u2192 Secrets: `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY` and `OPENAI_API_KEY`, both attached to this notebook. Never paste a key into a cell. A missing key just skips that provider. Set `OPENAI_MODEL` to a chat model your key can use: nothing is selected automatically, and while it is blank the notebook prints the model ids your key can use and skips OpenAI.\n",
    "\n",
    "**If Run All stops part-way in the editor,** run the remaining cells from the top down by hand; each cell is independent of how it was started. The last cell lists every command that failed.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Time and quota.** The API work runs in the background while the GPU trains, so the full run is expected to take roughly 4 to 6 hours of GPU session time (an estimate: it has not been timed on Kaggle). The run stops itself after `DEADLINE_HOURS` and packs what it has; interrupted API jobs resume if you run again with the same outputs. Keep `DEADLINE_HOURS` below your remaining weekly quota: a run that Kaggle kills for quota may lose its output.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Cost.** The API calls are billed by the providers. Per provider, experiment 1 makes about 2,000 short requests per view (571 records; 1,461 decision steps) and experiment 4 about 15 requests per session. The trial prints the measured tokens per session, so you can scale it to `MAS_SESSIONS` before the full run."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "metadata": {},
   "execution_count": null,
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "TRIAL = True                 # True: 10-minute check of keys and code. False: the full run (use Save & Run All).\n",
    "DEADLINE_HOURS = 8.0         # the full run stops starting new work after this many hours and packs what it has\n",
    "\n",
    "# experiment 1: LLM guards on R-Judge\n",
    "CLAUDE_MODEL = \"claude-opus-5-5\"\n",
    "CLAUDE_EFFORT = \"medium\"\n",
    "OPENAI_MODEL = \"\"            # e.g. the id of a current chat model on your account; \"\" skips everything OpenAI\n",
    "LOCAL_MODEL = \"Qwen/Qwen2.5-7B-Instruct\"     # \"\" skips the local guard\n",
    "SPLITS = 100                 # splits per protocol for the trained scorers (experiments 2 and 3)\n",
    "\n",
    "# experiment 4: multi-agent traces\n",
    "MAS_CLAUDE_MODEL = \"claude-opus-5-5\"   # the Claude model that plays the agents; \"\" skips. Any Claude model id works.\n",
    "MAS_CLAUDE_EFFORT = \"low\"\n",
    "MAS_OPENAI_MODEL = OPENAI_MODEL        # the OpenAI model that plays the agents; \"\" skips\n",
    "MAS_SESSIONS = 400           # sessions per agent model\n",
    "MAS_SPLITS = 50\n",
    "MAS_WORKERS = 8              # sessions generated in parallel per provider\n",
    "\n",
    "import os, signal, subprocess, time\n",
    "T0 = time.time()\n",
    "os.makedirs(\"/kaggle/temp\", exist_ok=True)       # scratch space; only the zip goes to /kaggle/working\n",
    "os.chdir(\"/kaggle/temp\")\n",
    "os.environ[\"PYTHONUNBUFFERED\"] = \"1\"\n",
    "FAILED = []\n",
    "def sh(cmd):\n",
    "    print(\"$\", cmd, flush=True)\n",
    "    get_ipython().system(cmd)\n",
    "    code = get_ipython().user_ns.get(\"_exit_code\", 0)\n",
    "    if code:\n",
    "        FAILED.append(cmd)\n",
    "        print(f\"!! exit code {code}: this command failed; later stages still run\", flush=True)\n",
    "    return code\n",
    "if not os.path.exists(\"/kaggle/temp/CV\"):\n",
    "    sh(\"git clone -q --depth 1 -b claude/implement-conformalguard-UGndd https://example.org/anonymous")\n",
    "    sh(\"git clone -q --depth 1 https://github.com/Lordog/R-Judge.git\")\n",
    "    sh(\"git clone -q --depth 1 https://github.com/uiuc-kang-lab/InjecAgent.git\")\n",
    "    sh(\"pip -q install sentence-transformers scikit-learn pytest accelerate anthropic openai\")\n",
    "os.chdir(\"/kaggle/temp/CV/ConformalGuard\")\n",
    "sh(\"git log --oneline -1\")\n",
    "RJ, IA = \"../../R-Judge\", \"../../InjecAgent\"\n",
    "RUNS = \"runs_trial\" if TRIAL else \"runs\"\n",
    "QUICK = \"--quick\" if TRIAL else \"\"\n",
    "ZIP = \"/kaggle/working/\" + (\"rjudge_extra_TRIAL.zip\" if TRIAL else \"rjudge_extra_results.zip\")\n",
    "os.makedirs(f\"{RUNS}/logs\", exist_ok=True)\n",
    "\n",
    "def pack():\n",
    "    sh(f\"cd /kaggle/temp/CV/ConformalGuard && zip -qr {ZIP} {RUNS} -x '*/cache/*' && ls -la {ZIP}\")\n",
    "def hours():\n",
    "    return (time.time() - T0) / 3600\n",
    "def time_left(stage):\n",
    "    if TRIAL or hours() < DEADLINE_HOURS:\n",
    "        return True\n",
    "    print(f\"SKIPPED {stage}: {hours():.1f} h elapsed, past DEADLINE_HOURS = {DEADLINE_HOURS}\")\n",
    "    return False"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "metadata": {},
   "execution_count": null,
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# API keys come from Kaggle Secrets and are only placed in this process's environment.\n",
    "try:\n",
    "    from kaggle_secrets import UserSecretsClient\n",
    "    _secrets = UserSecretsClient()\n",
    "    for _k in (\"ANTHROPIC_API_KEY\", \"OPENAI_API_KEY\"):\n",
    "        try:\n",
    "            os.environ[_k] = _secrets.get_secret(_k)\n",
    "            print(_k, \"loaded\")\n",
    "        except Exception:\n",
    "            print(_k, \"not set: that provider will be skipped\")\n",
    "except ImportError:\n",
    "    print(\"not on Kaggle: using keys already in the environment, if any\")\n",
    "HAVE_CLAUDE = bool(os.environ.get(\"ANTHROPIC_API_KEY\"))\n",
    "HAVE_OPENAI = bool(os.environ.get(\"OPENAI_API_KEY\")) and bool(OPENAI_MODEL)\n",
    "print(\"Claude:\", \"on\" if HAVE_CLAUDE else \"off\", \"| OpenAI:\", \"on\" if HAVE_OPENAI else \"off (set OPENAI_MODEL and the secret)\")\n",
    "if os.environ.get(\"OPENAI_API_KEY\") and not OPENAI_MODEL:\n",
    "    print(\"\\nOPENAI_MODEL is blank, so everything OpenAI is skipped. Nothing is chosen automatically.\")\n",
    "    print(\"Copy one of the ids below into OPENAI_MODEL in the first code cell and run again:\")\n",
    "    sh(\"python scripts/openai_list_models.py\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
