   "source": [
    "## 0. Sanity check (all tests must pass)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "metadata": {},
   "execution_count": null,
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "sh(\"python -m pytest tests/test_core.py tests/test_adaptive.py tests/test_rjudge.py tests/test_guards.py tests/test_mas.py -q\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## API jobs: session generation (experiment 4) and LLM judges (experiment 1)\n",
    "\n",
    "One job chain per provider: first the multi-agent sessions, then the R-Judge judge in both views. In the full run the chains work in the background while the GPU stages below train; their output goes to `runs/logs/`. In the trial they run here, in the foreground, on a handful of records and sessions.\n",
    "\n",
    "Server-side refusal fallbacks are on for the Claude calls, so a request declined by the safety classifiers is re-run on a fallback model; the outputs record which model served each row or session."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "metadata": {},
   "execution_count": null,
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "LIMIT = \"--limit 5\" if TRIAL else \"\"\n",
    "N_MAS = 4 if TRIAL else MAS_SESSIONS\n",
    "PASSES = 1 if TRIAL else 2            # the second pass retries calls and sessions that failed\n",
    "\n",
    "def claude_chain():\n",
    "    cmds = []\n",
    "    if MAS_CLAUDE_MODEL:\n",
    "        cmds += [f\"python scripts/mas_generate_claude.py --model {MAS_CLAUDE_MODEL} --effort {MAS_CLAUDE_EFFORT} --n {N_MAS} \"\n",
    "                 f\"--seed-start 0 --workers {MAS_WORKERS} --out {RUNS}/mas_claude\"] * PASSES\n",
    "    cmds += [f\"touch {RUNS}/logs/mas_claude.done\"]\n",
    "    for mode in (\"causal\", \"full\"):\n",
    "        cmds += [f\"python scripts/rjudge_judge_claude.py --rjudge-dir {RJ} --model {CLAUDE_MODEL} --effort {CLAUDE_EFFORT} \"\n",
    "                 f\"--mode {mode} {LIMIT} --out {RUNS}/guard_claude_{mode}\"] * PASSES\n",
    "    return cmds\n",
    "\n",
    "def openai_chain():\n",
    "    cmds = []\n",
    "    if MAS_OPENAI_MODEL:\n",
    "        cmds += [f\"python scripts/mas_generate_openai.py --model {MAS_OPENAI_MODEL} --n {N_MAS} \"\n",
    "                 f\"--seed-start 100000 --workers {MAS_WORKERS} --out {RUNS}/mas_openai\"] * PASSES\n",
    "    cmds += [f\"touch {RUNS}/logs/mas_openai.done\"]\n",
    "    for mode in (\"causal\", \"full\"):\n",
    "        cmds += [f\"python scripts/rjudge_judge_openai.py --rjudge-dir {RJ} --model {OPENAI_MODEL} \"\n",
    "                 f\"--mode {mode} {LIMIT} --out {RUNS}/guard_openai_{mode}\"] * PASSES\n",
    "    return cmds\n",
    "\n",
    "CHAINS = {}\n",
    "if HAVE_CLAUDE: CHAINS[\"claude\"] = claude_chain()\n",
    "if HAVE_OPENAI: CHAINS[\"openai\"] = openai_chain()\n",
    "JOBS = {}\n",
    "for name, cmds in CHAINS.items():\n",
    "    if TRIAL:\n",
    "        for c in cmds:\n",
    "            sh(c)\n",
    "    else:\n",
    "        log = open(f\"{RUNS}/logs/{name}.log\", \"w\")\n",
    "        JOBS[name] = subprocess.Popen([\"bash\", \"-c\", \" ; \".join(cmds)], stdout=log, stderr=subprocess.STDOUT,\n",
    "                                      start_new_session=True)\n",
    "        print(f\"started the {name} chain in the background ({len(cmds)} commands); log: {RUNS}/logs/{name}.log\")\n",
    "\n",
    "def status():\n",
    "    for name, p in JOBS.items():\n",
    "        state = \"running\" if p.poll() is None else f\"finished (exit {p.returncode})\"\n",
    "        print(f\"[{hours():.1f} h] {name} chain {state}; last lines of its log:\")\n",
    "        sh(f\"tail -n 3 {RUNS}/logs/{name}.log\")\n",
    "\n",
    "def wait_for(done, what):\n",
    "    # wait until done() is true, every chain has ended, or the deadline has passed\n",
    "    while not done() and any(p.poll() is None for p in JOBS.values()) and hours() < DEADLINE_HOURS:\n",
    "        time.sleep(60)\n",
    "    print(f\"[{hours():.1f} h] stopped waiting for {what}\"); status()\n",
    "\n",
    "if TRIAL:\n",
    "    files = \" \".join(f for f in (f\"{RUNS}/mas_claude/sessions.jsonl\", f\"{RUNS}/mas_openai/sessions.jsonl\") if os.path.exists(f))\n",
    "    if files:\n",
    "        print(\"\\nOne generated session per agent model. Read it: do the agents do sensible things?\")\n",
    "        print(\"If the 'refused steps' count in a usage line above is more than a few, or the steps below\")\n",
    "        print(\"read '(declined)', do NOT start the full run: paste this output to get it fixed first.\\n\")\n",
    "        for f in files.split():\n",
    "            sh(f\"python scripts/mas_show.py {f} --session 0\")\n",
    "    pack()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 2. Step-level guarantee on the injection records"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "metadata": {},
   "execution_count": null,
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "if time_left(\"experiment 2\"):\n",
    "    sh(f\"python scripts/rjudge_steps.py --rjudge-dir {RJ} --injecagent-dir {IA} --features st --reps {SPLITS} {QUICK} --out {RUNS}/rjudge_steps\")\n",
    "    pack(); status()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 3. In-domain recalibration and per-category calibration"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "metadata": {},
   "execution_count": null,
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "if time_left(\"experiment 3\"):\n",
    "    sh(f\"python scripts/rjudge_run.py --rjudge-dir {RJ} --features st --protocols random,recal --reps {SPLITS} --loco-reps 20 {QUICK} --out {RUNS}/rjudge_recal_minilm\")\n",
    "    pack(); status()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 4. Multi-agent trace experiment\n",
    "\n",
    "Waits for the session generation to finish, shows what was generated, then trains and evaluates the scorers. In the trial there are too few sessions to train on, so this stage only runs in the full run (its code path is covered by the tests in stage 0)."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "metadata": {},
   "execution_count": null,
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "MAS_FILES = [f for f in (f\"{RUNS}/mas_claude/sessions.jsonl\", f\"{RUNS}/mas_openai/sessions.jsonl\")]\n",
    "if TRIAL:\n",
    "    print(\"Nothing to do in the trial: 4 sessions per model are too few to train on. This stage runs in the full run.\")\n",
    "if not TRIAL:\n",
    "    wait_for(lambda: all(os.path.exists(f\"{RUNS}/logs/mas_{n}.done\") for n in JOBS), \"session generation\")\n",
    "    files = \" \".join(f for f in MAS_FILES if os.path.exists(f))\n",
    "    if files and time_left(\"experiment 4\"):\n",
    "        sh(f\"python scripts/mas_show.py {files}\")\n",
    "        sh(f\"python scripts/mas_run.py --sessions {files} --features st --reps {MAS_SPLITS} --out {RUNS}/mas_exp\")\n",
    "    pack()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 1a. Local model as a guard (GPU, one forward pass per unit)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "metadata": {},
   "execution_count": null,
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "if TRIAL:\n",
    "    print(\"Skipped in the trial (it downloads a 15 GB model and needs the GPU). It runs in the full run.\")\n",
    "if LOCAL_MODEL and not TRIAL and time_left(\"the local guard\"):\n",
    "    for mode in (\"causal\", \"full\"):\n",
    "        sh(f\"python scripts/rjudge_judge_local.py --rjudge-dir {RJ} --model {LOCAL_MODEL} --mode {mode} --out {RUNS}/guard_local_{mode}\")\n",
    "    pack(); status()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 1d. Wait for the API judges, then calibrate every guard's scores (CPU, a few minutes)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "metadata": {},
   "execution_count": null,
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "if not TRIAL:\n",
    "    wait_for(lambda: False, \"the API judges\")\n",
    "    for name, p in JOBS.items():\n",
    "        if p.poll() is None:\n",
    "            os.killpg(p.pid, signal.SIGTERM)       # the chain and the script it is running\n",
    "            print(f\"{name} chain stopped at the deadline; its partial outputs are kept and resume on a rerun\")\n",
    "specs = \" \".join(f\"{name}_{mode}={RUNS}/guard_{name}_{mode}/scores.jsonl\"\n",
    "                 for name in (\"local\", \"claude\", \"openai\") for mode in (\"causal\", \"full\")\n",
    "                 if os.path.exists(f\"{RUNS}/guard_{name}_{mode}/scores.jsonl\"))\n",
    "if specs and not TRIAL:\n",
    "    sh(f\"python scripts/rjudge_guard_eval.py --rjudge-dir {RJ} --scores {specs} --reps 1000 --out {RUNS}/guard_eval\")\n",
    "pack()\n",
    "if FAILED:\n",
    "    print(f\"{len(FAILED)} command(s) FAILED; scroll up to their output:\")\n",
    "    for c in FAILED:\n",
    "        print(\"  \", c)\n",
    "else:\n",
    "    print(\"every command exited normally\")\n",
    "print(f\"finished after {hours():.2f} h. \" + (\"TRIAL outputs are smoke runs, not results. If both providers answered above, set TRIAL = False and use Save & Run All.\"\n",
    "                                             if TRIAL else \"Download rjudge_extra_results.zip from this version's Output tab.\"))"
   ]
  }
